1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,508
Embassy Bancorp's third quarter: the
fastest profit growth of three

2
00:00:04,508 --> 00:00:07,118
Pennsylvania banks, on the thinnest
margin.

3
00:00:07,668 --> 00:00:13,219
Earnings were sixty-six cents a
share, up thirty-two percent from a
year ago. No analyst covers this

4
00:00:13,219 --> 00:00:16,075
stock, so there is no estimate to
compare with.

5
00:00:16,625 --> 00:00:22,383
Net income was four point nine
million dollars, up twenty-eight
percent. That was the fastest growth

6
00:00:22,383 --> 00:00:24,807
of three Pennsylvania community
banks.

7
00:00:25,357 --> 00:00:30,825
The bank's margin widened
thirty-two basis points to two point
eight four percent. But the two peers

8
00:00:30,825 --> 00:00:35,595
run at three point eight six and four
point five four, so it is still the
thinnest.

9
00:00:36,145 --> 00:00:42,486
The open question is the balance
sheet. Unrealized losses on securities
reached sixty-six million dollars, and

10
00:00:42,486 --> 00:00:46,082
with buybacks, equity fell almost
eight percent this year.

11
00:00:46,632 --> 00:00:52,481
Net interest income did most of the
work, adding one point eight million
dollars as funding costs fell.

12
00:00:52,481 --> 00:00:57,248
Expenses took back about half a
million, and taxes about three
hundred thousand.

13
00:00:57,798 --> 00:01:03,514
Watch three things next quarter.
Whether funding costs keep falling.
How bond prices move the securities

14
00:01:03,514 --> 00:01:07,182
losses. And whether the margin
keeps closing the gap to peers.

15
00:01:07,732 --> 00:01:11,840
Embassy, based in Bethlehem, is
growing profit quickly. The question

16
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:14,665
is whether a thin margin can keep
widening.

